oxy - rejected\n   - Adding `expectedSessionID` field - rejected\n   - Pre-binding session_id during proxy registration - user questioned it\n\n8. User provided definitive backend log evidence showing the root cause:\n```\n12:35:16 trace-init: session=ddd6a79e-... bound to proxy pid=26292  ← Correct\n12:35:23 trace-init: session=ae44a20e-... bound to proxy pid=26292  ← WRONG! Should be pid=17600\n```\n\n9. The backend's `TraceInit` broadcast routes trace-init to the WRONG proxy. When two proxies run concurrently, the broadcast tries proxies in random map order, and the first one to respond wins - regardless of which proxy should handle which session.\n\n10. I confirmed the guard approach (reject trace-init if p.sessionID already set with different value) handles all 4 scenarios correctly.\n\n11. User's latest question asks about two alternative approaches:\n    - \"设计成串行启动的\" - design as serial/sequential startup\n    - \"预设表示为，在内部添加一个表示的去进行pid的匹配\" - pre-set an identifier internally for PID matching\n\nKey files examined:\n- `claude_tap_plus/cmd/claude-tap/main.go` - proxy startup/shutdown, buildResumeCommand\n- `claude_tap_plus/internal/proxy/reverse.go` - ReverseProxy struct, handleTraceInit\n- `claude_tap_plus/internal/backend/api/proxy_handler.go` - TraceInit routing, broadcast logic\n- `claude_tap_plus/cmd/claude-tap/backend_autostart.go` - ensureBackend, registerProxyWithBackend\n- `claude_tap_plus/cmd/claude-tap/session_files.go` - proxy.json management\n- `.claude/hooks/01-session-start/base.sh` - hook session registration\n- `.claude/hooks/base.sh` - HOOK_INPUT, json_get\n- `.claude/hooks/lib/backend.sh` - _call_backend, _backend_available\n\nNo code changes were successfully made - all edits were rejected by the user.\n</analysis>\n\n<summary>\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   User discovered that when running two `claude-tap-plus` instances concurrently with different `--resume` session IDs, the trace-init routing in the backend sends session initialization to the WRONG proxy process, causing:\n   - The wrong proxy gets its `p.sessionID` overwritten with the other session's ID\n   - The correct proxy never receives its trace-init, resulting in no Trace file and no Resume output\n   - The `buildResumeCommand` in main.go generates a Resume command with the wrong session ID\n   \n   User wants to fix the routing so that each proxy instance is isolated - each session_id maps to exactly one proxy, and trace-init is routed correctly.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - **claude-tap-plus architecture**: Two trees - `.claude/` (shell hooks/skills) and `claude_tap_plus/` (Go proxy+backend). Communicate over HTTP on 127.0.0.1.\n   - **Proxy lifecycle**: `runProxy()` in main.go creates `rp` (ReverseProxy), starts HTTP server, registers with backend, starts Claude Code as child process\n   - **trace-init flow**: Hook `01-session-start` → `_call_backend \"/api/proxy/trace-init\"` → Backend `ProxyHandler.TraceInit()` → broadcast to all proxies → `relayTraceInit()` → proxy's `/_internal/trace-init` → `handleTraceInit()` sets `p.sessionID`\n   - **Backend broadcast routing**: When session_id is not pre-bound, backend iterates ALL registered proxies and relays trace-init to each; first success wins. Go map iteration order is random.\n   - **HOOK_INPUT sharing**: `base.sh` reads stdin once into `HOOK_INPUT`, both `init_trace_path()` and `register_session()` use `json_get '.session_id'` from same `HOOK_INPUT`\n   - **Session ID sources**: Hook stdin JSON (used for trace-init and session/register), API request metadata.user_id (extracted by `extractSessionID()`), and `p.sessionID` (set by trace-init, used for Resume command)\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - **`claude_tap_plus/cmd/claude-tap/main.go`**\n     - `runProxy()`: main proxy lifecycle - parses args, creates `rp`, starts proxy, registers with backend, starts Claude Code, waits, generates summary and Resume command\n     - `buildResumeCommand(originalArgs, sessionID)`: removes old `--resume` from originalArgs, appends `--resume sessionID` - currently uses `rp.SessionID()` (from trace-init) which can be wrong\n     - `originalArgs` saved at line 116 for Resume command generation\n     - Lines 371-377: Resume command generation using `rp.SessionID()`\n     \n   - **`claude_tap_plus/internal/proxy/reverse.go`**\n     - `ReverseProxy` struct (lines 22-41): contains `sessionID string` field set by trace-init\n     - `handleTraceInit()` (lines 488-557): accepts ANY trace-init request, sets `p.sessionID = req.SessionID` without guard. Overwrites previous value if called again.\n     - Key vulnerable code at line 531: `p.sessionID = req.SessionID` - no protection against overwrite\n     \n   - **`claude_tap_plus/internal/backend/api/proxy_handler.go`**\n     - `ProxyHandler` struct: `proxies map[string]string` (pid→url), `sessions map[string]string` (session_id→url), `proxySessions map[string][]string` (pid→[]session_id)\n     - `TraceInit()` (lines 133-203): Checks `sessions` map for direct route; if not found, broadcasts to ALL registered proxies. **Root cause**: broadcast tries proxies in random order, first success wins regardless of correctness.\n     - `relayTraceInit()` (lines 252-277): Forwards trace-init to a single proxy URL\n     - Broadcast loop (lines 186-199): iterates `proxiesCopy`, first successful `relayTraceInit` wins\n     \n   - **`claude_tap_plus/cmd/claude-tap/backend_autostart.go`**\n     - `registerProxyWithBackend(proxyURL)`: registers proxy with backend, only sends `pid` and `proxy_url` - no session_id\n     - `ensureBackend()`: checks if backend running, starts if not\n     - `unregisterProxyFromBackend()`: unregisters proxy by pid\n     \n   - **`.claude/hooks/01-session-start/base.sh`**\n     - `init_trace_path()`: calls `_call_backend \"/api/proxy/trace-init\"` with session_id from `json_get '.session_id'`\n     - `register_session()`: calls `_call_backend \"/api/session/register\"` with same session_id\n     - Both use same `HOOK_INPUT` variable\n     \n   - **`.claude/hooks/base.sh`**\n     - `HOOK_INPUT=$(cat)`: reads stdin once\n     - `json_get()`: parses from `HOOK_INPUT` using jq/python/sed\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - **Misidentified as encoding/garbled text**: Initially thought emoji characters (📋📎🚀) were causing Windows terminal corruption. User corrected: \"这个不是乱码的问题，是两个session id 不一致\"\n   - **Wrong command mapping**: Initially mapped Command 1 as `--resume ae44a20e-...` but user corrected: Command 1 was `--resume ddd6a79e-...`, Command 2 was `--resume ae44a20e-...`\n   - **Proposed expectedSessionID field**: Added field to ReverseProxy struct, user rejected - said objects should be isolated per process\n   - **Proposed traceInitOnce guard**: User said objects are already isolated, not shared\n   - **Proposed pre-binding during registration**: User asked \"如果不存在session_id的时候呢\" - pointed out it doesn't work for non-resume cases\n   - **User consistently said**: Fix is about `rp` variable being shared through HTTP exposure, not about process isolation\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - **Confirmed root cause with definitive log evidence**:\n     ```\n     trace-init: session=ddd6a79e-... bound to proxy pid=26292  ← Correct (Command 1)\n     trace-init: session=ae44a20e-... bound to proxy pid=26292  ← WRONG! Should be pid=17600 (Command 2)\n     ```\n   - Backend's `TraceInit` broadcast routes trace-init to wrong proxy when multiple proxies are registered\n   - **Verified guard approach handles all 4 scenarios**: both with resume, both without, first with/second without, first without/second with - all work correctly because wrong proxy rejects and backend tries next\n   - User is now evaluating two alternative approaches: serial startup design vs. internal PID matching identifier\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - \"存在claude --resume eeb8e205-... 这个问题的，我认为是main.go需要从这个里面进行对应的排查的\"\n   - \"这个不是乱码的问题，是两个session id 不一致，claude code 和claude_tap_plus\"\n   - \"你先搞清楚注册的一个逻辑的。他是和hook配合这来的 01-session-start/base.sh 和这个配合来的\"\n   - \"我刚刚测试了一下就是... 这个命令之后，就会出现Resume this session with: claude --resume ddd6a79e-... 这段输出和对应的log\"\n   - \"我认为是hooks存在共享的变量的，你理解么？\"\n   - \"不是这样的，我的意思是它是把session_id当作一个共享的变量了，不是从钩子输入里面获取的\"\n   - \"main.go的逻辑是什么呢？？？？在这个情况下进行推理的\"\n   - \"里面的rp是不是共享的呢？\"\n   - \"我希望的是他不是共享变量，每一次的启动都是一个单独的变量的\"\n   - \"我想的是每一次的命令启动都是一个单独的 claude_tap_plus进程的。里面的对象是隔离的，不是共享的\"\n   - \"是main.go里面的方法rp变量共享了\"\n   - \"hook没有错的，第一次... 对得上，然后第二次... 注册这里的session_id... 最后/exit命令调用后端接口是... 这一段的，还有就是Resume这段是main.go里面的\"\n   - \"是main.go里面的方法rp变量共享了\"\n   - (Provided definitive backend log showing trace-init bound to wrong pid=26292 instead of pid=17600)\n   - \"这里存在一个问题就是在trace_init的时候在同一个pid里面去了，不是根据session_id来的，应该是一个个session_id 一个proxy的\"\n   - \"如果不存在session_id的时候呢？？你这样做，如果没有session_id的时候直接启动的时候会不会收到影响的呢？\"\n   - \"还有两个场景，就是先有--resume，后是没有，还有一个就是先没有后有--resume的场景的\"\n   - \"设计成串行启动的呢？？或者预设表示为，在内部添加一个表示的去进行pid的匹配的可以完成么？\"\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Fix the trace-init routing issue so each proxy only receives its own session's trace-init\n   - User is evaluating two approaches: (1) serial startup design, (2) internal identifier for PID matching\n   - No code changes have been successfully applied yet\n\n8. Current Work:\n   User asked about two alternative design approaches for the fix:\n   - \"设计成串行启动的呢\" — design as serial/sequential startup (ensure only one proxy runs at a time)\n   - \"预设表示为，在内部添加一个表示的去进行pid的匹配的可以完成么\" — pre-set an identifier internally in the proxy for PID matching during trace-init routing\n   \n   The conversation was at the point of evaluating which approach to implement. The guard approach (reject trace-init if p.sessionID already set) was confirmed to handle all 4 scenarios, but user wants to consider these alternative approaches before committing to a fix.\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Respond to user's question about the two alternative approaches:\n   1. **Serial startup**: Ensure only one proxy runs at a time - analyze feasibility and implications\n   2. **Internal PID matching identifier**: Add an internal identifier to the proxy that gets included in trace-init routing - analyze how this would work with the backend's existing routing logic\n   \n   User's exact question: \"设计成串行启动的呢？？或者预设表示为，在内部添加一个表示的去进行pid的匹配的可以完成么？\"\n</summary>","background_tasks":[],"session_crons":[]}
