[2026-06-07 13:03:27] [INFO] [SubagentStop] Input: {"session_id":"5a952b88-dbcf-40a5-820e-fed7478f0486","transcript_path":"C:\\Users\\Administrator\\.claude\\projects\\D--CodeDevelopment-CodeProject-claude-hk\\5a952b88-dbcf-40a5-820e-fed7478f0486.jsonl","cwd":"D:\\CodeDevelopment\\CodeProject\\claude-hk","permission_mode":"default","agent_id":"a86466fc76856b101","agent_type":"Explore","hook_event_name":"SubagentStop","stop_hook_active":false,"agent_transcript_path":"C:\\Users\\Administrator\\.claude\\projects\\D--CodeDevelopment-CodeProject-claude-hk\\5a952b88-dbcf-40a5-820e-fed7478f0486\\subagents\\agent-a86466fc76856b101.jsonl","last_assistant_message":"Based on my analysis of the codebase, here's how Kimi is configured as an API provider in claude_tap_plus:\n\n## Kimi Configuration in claude_tap_plus\n\n### 1. **Profile Configuration Structure**\nKimi is configured through the `profiles.json` file located at `~/.claude-tap-plus/profiles.json`. The structure supports:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"default\": \"kimi-profile\",\n  \"profiles\": {\n    \"kimi-profile\": {\n      \"base_url\": \"https://api.moonshot.cn/v1\",\n      \"api_key\": \"your-kimi-api-key\",\n      \"provider\": \"anthropic\",\n      \"model\": \"kimi-k2\"\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\n### 2. **Key Configuration Components**\n\n#### **ProfileConfig Structure** (from `config/profiles.go`)\n```go\ntype ProfileConfig struct {\n    BaseURL   string `json:\"base_url\"`              // API endpoint URL\n    APIKey    string `json:\"api_key\"`               // API key for authentication\n    AuthToken string `json:\"auth_token,omitempty\"`  // OAuth token\n    Provider  string `json:\"provider,omitempty\"`    // Provider identifier (anthropic/openai/gemini)\n    Model     string `json:\"model,omitempty\"`       // Override model name\n}\n```\n\n### 3. **Kimi-Specific Features**\n\n#### **Kimi Mode Detection**\nThe system automatically detects if the upstream API is Kimi/Moonshot by checking if the URL contains \"kimi\" or \"moonshot\":\n\n```go\nfunc IsKimiURL(url string) bool {\n    lower := strings.ToLower(url)\n    return strings.Contains(lower, \"kimi\") || strings.Contains(lower, \"moonshot\")\n}\n```\n\n#### **Kimi Mode Activation**\nWhen Kimi is detected:\n- Enables `reasoning_content` caching\n- Special handling for Kimi's reasoning content in responses\n\n```go\n// In main.go:\nif proxy.IsKimiURL(resolved.BaseURL) {\n    rp.SetKimiMode(true)\n}\n```\n\n#### **Reasoning Content Caching**\nKimi mode activates special caching for `reasoning_content` fields in responses:\n\n```go\ntype ReverseProxy struct {\n    reasoningCache     *ReasoningCache     // reasoning_content caching (Kimi mode only)\n    kimiMode           bool                // Whether it's a Kimi upstream\n}\n```\n\n### 4. **Configuration Resolution Priority**\n\nThe system follows this priority chain for configuration:\n1. Command line arguments (highest)\n2. `profiles.json` named profile\n3. Default profile from `profiles.json`\n4. Claude's `~/.claude/settings.json` (fallback)\n\n### 5. **Kimi Model Support**\n\nFrom the test files, Kimi supports models like:\n- `kimi-k2`\n- `kimi-for-coding`\n- Other Kimi-specific models\n\nThe system will preserve these model names when configured in profiles.json.\n\n### 6. **Usage**\n\nTo use Kimi:\n1. Create a profile in `~/.claude-tap-plus/profiles.json`\n2. Set `base_url` to Kimi's API endpoint (e.g., `https://api.moonshot.cn/v1`)\n3. Provide your Kimi API key\n4. Optionally specify the Kimi model name\n5. Use the profile with `--tap-profile kimi-profile`\n\nThe system will automatically detect Kimi URLs and enable the special reasoning content caching functionality.","background_tasks":[],"session_crons":[]}
