[2026-06-07 18:42:33] [INFO] [SubagentStop] Input: {"session_id":"5a952b88-dbcf-40a5-820e-fed7478f0486","transcript_path":"C:\\Users\\Administrator\\.claude\\projects\\D--CodeDevelopment-CodeProject-claude-hk\\5a952b88-dbcf-40a5-820e-fed7478f0486.jsonl","cwd":"D:\\CodeDevelopment\\CodeProject\\claude-hk\\claude_tap_plus","permission_mode":"acceptEdits","agent_id":"a8516f30da5839fe3","agent_type":"","effort":{"level":"medium"},"hook_event_name":"SubagentStop","stop_hook_active":false,"agent_transcript_path":"C:\\Users\\Administrator\\.claude\\projects\\D--CodeDevelopment-CodeProject-claude-hk\\5a952b88-dbcf-40a5-820e-fed7478f0486\\subagents\\agent-a8516f30da5839fe3.jsonl","last_assistant_message":"<analysis>\nLet me chronologically analyze the conversation:\n\n1. The conversation started with a continuation from a previous session about fixing trace-init routing in claude_tap_plus when multiple proxy instances run concurrently.\n\n2. The user asked about the shared data architecture of the entire system - what data is shared, how it's separated, and which part belongs to Kimi. I explored the codebase and provided a comprehensive map of all shared data points.\n\n3. The user then asked about the PID matching approach we had discussed before compaction. I explained the two approaches (serial startup vs PID matching) and the user seemed to lean toward PID matching.\n\n4. The user pointed out that hooks run in the local Windows environment, not inside the claued_tap_plus.exe process. This led to a discussion about environment variable propagation through the process chain.\n\n5. The user was concerned about env vars not reaching hooks since hooks are spawned by Claude Code, not by claued_tap_plus.exe directly.\n\n6. After much discussion about env vars vs file-based approaches, the user proposed their own design: a file-based PID mechanism with locking - one PID file slot, lock, read-once-delete. This became the accepted approach.\n\n7. I implemented the changes across 4 files:\n   - `main.go`: File lock (mkdir), PID file write, block waiting for trace-init, release lock\n   - `reverse.go`: OnTraceInitDone callback, guard (reject wrong session trace-init)\n   - `base.sh`: Read .init-pid, include proxy_pid in trace-init, delete file\n   - `proxy_handler.go`: traceMu serial lock, proxy_pid precise routing\n   - `request.go`: Added ProxyPID field to TraceInitRequest\n\n8. First test: exe wasn't rebuilt. I rebuilt with `go build -o claued_tap_plus.exe ./cmd/claude-tap`.\n\n9. Second test: The guard in reverse.go was too strict - it rejected legitimate session updates when the user ran `claude` directly (without claued_tap_plus.exe). I removed the strict guard and replaced it with just a debug log.\n\n10. Third test: The user ran two concurrent claued_tap_plus.exe instances AND used `/clear` command in Claude Code. The `/clear` command generates a NEW session_id (fa456378), different from the original (ae44a20e). The new session_id's trace-init went via broadcast (no PID) because no new proxy was started for the /clear session.\n\nKey finding: `/clear` in Claude Code creates a new session_id within the SAME proxy process. The proxy already has sessionID set from the original trace-init, and the new trace-init for the /clear session goes via broadcast because no new .init-pid was written.\n\nThe current issue is: `/clear` creates a new session_id but the proxy's sessionID doesn't update because:\n1. No new .init-pid is written (proxy is already running, not restarting)\n2. The new trace-init goes via broadcast\n3. The broadcast may route to the wrong proxy\n\nFiles modified (committed as 57b5a7d):\n- `claude_tap_plus/cmd/claude-tap/main.go`\n- `claude_tap_plus/internal/proxy/reverse.go`\n- `claude_tap_plus/internal/backend/api/proxy_handler.go`\n- `claude_tap_plus/internal/backend/api/request.go`\n- `.claude/hooks/01-session-start/base.sh`\n\nThen an additional uncommitted change to reverse.go: removed the strict guard (reject on sessionID mismatch) and replaced with just a debug log line.\n\nThe user's latest message reveals the root cause of the remaining issue: `/clear` command changes the session_id within an already-running proxy session, and our init-lock + PID mechanism only handles the initial proxy startup, not mid-session session_id changes.\n</analysis>\n\n<summary>\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user wants to fix a bug where running multiple `claued_tap_plus.exe` instances concurrently causes trace-init routing to send session initialization to the WRONG proxy process. This results in:\n   - The wrong proxy getting its `p.sessionID` overwritten\n   - The `buildResumeCommand` generating a Resume command with the wrong session ID\n   - Trace files associated with wrong sessions\n   \n   The user also wants the fix to be compatible with Claude Code's `/clear` command, which generates a new session_id within an already-running proxy process.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - **claude_tap_plus architecture**: Two trees - `.claude/` (shell hooks/skills) and `claude_tap_plus/` (Go proxy+backend). Communicate over HTTP on 127.0.0.1.\n   - **Trace-init flow**: Hook `01-session-start` → `_call_backend \"/api/proxy/trace-init\"` → Backend `ProxyHandler.TraceInit()` → relay to proxy → `handleTraceInit()` sets `p.sessionID`\n   - **Init lock + PID file mechanism**: Proxy writes PID to `~/.claude-tap-plus/.init-pid` under a file lock (`mkdir .init-lock`), hook reads and deletes PID, sends trace-init with `proxy_pid`, backend routes precisely. Lock released after trace-init completes.\n   - **`/clear` command**: Claude Code's `/clear` command generates a BRAND NEW session_id within the same running proxy, triggering a new `01-session-start` hook event with a different session_id. This is incompatible with the current init-lock mechanism which only handles initial proxy startup.\n   - **Kimi mode**: Special upstream provider (Moonshot) with `reasoning_content` caching in proxy. All Kimi data is per-proxy-isolated (`sync.RWMutex` protected).\n   - **Shared data architecture**: `backend.json` (config bridge), `proxy.json` (session registry), `profiles.json` (API profiles), Backend in-memory maps (proxies/sessions/proxySessions with RWMutex), SQLite tables (machines/projects/sessions/issue_claims/config/proxies)\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - **`claude_tap_plus/cmd/claude-tap/main.go`**\n     - Added `path/filepath` and `strconv` to imports\n     - Added init lock + PID file logic between `registerProxyWithBackend` and Claude Code launch\n     - Added `initDone` channel and `OnTraceInitDone` callback for trace-init completion signaling\n     - Added blocking wait after `cmd.Start()` with 30s timeout\n     ```go\n     // ---- Init 锁：串行化 trace-init，确保 PID 文件一对一消费 ----\n     initLockPath := filepath.Join(BaseDir(), \".init-lock\")\n     initPIDPath := filepath.Join(BaseDir(), \".init-pid\")\n     \n     for {\n         if err := os.Mkdir(initLockPath, 0o755); err == nil {\n             logger.Info(\"main\", \"init lock acquired\")\n             break\n         }\n         logger.Debug(\"main\", \"init lock busy, waiting...\")\n         time.Sleep(100 * time.Millisecond)\n     }\n     defer os.RemoveAll(initLockPath)\n     \n     if err := os.WriteFile(initPIDPath, []byte(strconv.Itoa(os.Getpid())), 0o644); err != nil {\n         logger.Warn(\"main\", \"write init-pid failed: %v\", err)\n     }\n     \n     initDone := make(chan struct{}, 1)\n     rp.OnTraceInitDone = func() {\n         select {\n         case initDone <- struct{}{}:\n         default:\n         }\n     }\n     ```\n     ```go\n     // After cmd.Start():\n     select {\n     case <-initDone:\n         logger.Info(\"main\", \"trace-init received, init lock releasing\")\n     case <-time.After(30 * time.Second):\n         logger.Warn(\"main\", \"trace-init timeout (30s), releasing init lock anyway\")\n     }\n     os.Remove(initPIDPath)\n     os.RemoveAll(initLockPath)\n     ```\n\n   - **`claude_tap_plus/internal/proxy/reverse.go`**\n     - Added `OnTraceInitDone func()` field to ReverseProxy struct\n     - Guard was initially strict (reject if sessionID already set), then relaxed to just a debug log\n     - Added callback invocation at end of handleTraceInit\n     ```go\n     // Current state (guard relaxed):\n     if p.sessionID != \"\" && p.sessionID != req.SessionID {\n         logger.Debug(\"proxy\", \"trace-init: rebinding session %s -> %s\", p.sessionID, req.SessionID)\n     }\n     ```\n     ```go\n     // At end of handleTraceInit:\n     if p.OnTraceInitDone != nil {\n         p.OnTraceInitDone()\n     }\n     ```\n\n   - **`claude_tap_plus/internal/backend/api/request.go`**\n     - Added `ProxyPID` field to TraceInitRequest\n     ```go\n     type TraceInitRequest struct {\n         SessionID      string `json:\"session_id\"`\n         ProxyPID       string `json:\"proxy_pid\"`       // 写入 .init-pid 的代理 PID（精确路由用）\n         MachineID      string `json:\"machine_id\"`\n         ProjectSlug    string `json:\"project_slug\"`\n         TranscriptPath string `json:\"transcript_path\"`\n     }\n     ```\n\n   - **`claude_tap_plus/internal/backend/api/proxy_handler.go`**\n     - Added `traceMu sync.Mutex` to ProxyHandler struct\n     - Rewrote TraceInit() with 3-tier routing: (1) proxy_pid precise route, (2) session_id binding, (3) broadcast fallback\n     - All under traceMu serial lock\n     ```go\n     type ProxyHandler struct {\n         mu            sync.RWMutex\n         proxies       map[string]string\n         sessions      map[string]string\n         proxySessions map[string][]string\n         traceMu       sync.Mutex          // trace-init 串行锁\n         svc           *service.ProxyService\n     }\n     ```\n\n   - **`.claude/hooks/01-session-start/base.sh`**\n     - Added .init-pid file reading in `init_trace_path()`\n     ```bash\n     # 读取 init-pid 文件（由 proxy 写入，读后即删）\n     local init_pid_file=\"$HOME/.claude-tap-plus/.init-pid\"\n     local tap_pid=\"\"\n     if [ -f \"$init_pid_file\" ]; then\n         tap_pid=$(cat \"$init_pid_file\" 2>/dev/null)\n         rm -f \"$init_pid_file\"\n         log \"INFO\" \"Init PID consumed: ${tap_pid:-empty}\"\n     fi\n     ```\n     - Added `\"proxy_pid\":\"$tap_pid\"` to the trace-init JSON body\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - **Strict guard blocked legitimate session updates**: The initial guard (`if p.sessionID != \"\" && p.sessionID != req.SessionID { reject }`) prevented the proxy from accepting new trace-init when the old session ended. This blocked `/clear` scenarios and direct `claude` runs. Fixed by replacing rejection with a debug log only.\n   - **Tab vs space indentation mismatch**: Edit tool failed because the Go file uses tabs but the edit string used spaces. Fixed by using the exact tab-indented content from the file.\n   - **Exe not rebuilt**: `go build ./...` only checks compilation, doesn't produce output binary. User was testing with old exe. Fixed by running `go build -o claued_tap_plus.exe ./cmd/claude-tap`.\n   - **`/clear` incompatibility (CURRENT ISSUE)**: Claude Code's `/clear` command generates a new session_id within the same running proxy. The new hook fires `01-session-start` again, but no new .init-pid is written (proxy is already running), so trace-init goes via broadcast to potentially the wrong proxy.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - **Concurrent proxy routing**: SOLVED for initial startup. PID file + init lock + precise routing works correctly for two concurrent `claued_tap_plus.exe` instances. Verified in backend log showing correct PID route for both sessions.\n   - **`/clear` session_id change**: UNSOLVED. When `/clear` is used inside Claude Code, a new session_id is generated. The hook fires again but there's no .init-pid file (already consumed), so trace-init goes via broadcast. This can route to the wrong proxy, causing sessionID mismatch. The user's latest test showed: Claude Code displays session `fa456378` (from /clear)