这个加上一个锁的，只有一个claude code 启动成功了，并且覆盖了对应的pid之后才可以进行后续操作的。还有就是为什么rp不可以每一个进程独享一个呢\" (PID matching with lock, and why can't rp be per-process isolated)\n   - \"支持并发么？\" (does it support concurrency)\n   - \"我的意思是环境变量加锁来完成的，加入锁机制，每一个只有一个可以读取到对应的一个环境变量，读完了就删除的\" (env var with lock, one can read one, delete after reading)\n   - \"开始修改的，但是hooks脚本好像是读的本地的呢\" (start modifying, but hooks read from local)\n   - \"hooks的运行环境不是本地的么？？？？在我win电脑上运行的，不是在进行环境里面运行的\" (hooks run in local Windows env, not inside proxy env)\n   - \"但是脚本的读取是在win的环境里面，不是claued_tap_plus.exe 这个里面的\" (scripts read from Windows env, not from inside claued_tap_plus.exe)\n   - \"这里就存在共享的问题的\" (there's a sharing problem here)\n   - \"还有一个问题就是proxy路由如何路由的呢？？？？这里的问题偏移了么？\" (how does proxy routing work, has the issue drifted?)\n   - \"我想的一个proxy启动的时候他会去这样的...\" (user's design: PID file with lock, check existence, write if not present, lock needed)\n   - \"pid里面只有一个对应的pid，只允许有一个，没有的锁住的\" (PID file has only ONE PID, locked if not available)\n   - \"git commit\" (commit the changes)\n   - \"还是不想的\" (still not right - showing old exe test results)\n   - \"还是一样的没有进行修改的呢\" (still the same, no change - with full backend log showing PID routing works for first two but third session goes broadcast)\n   - \"对的，我这里使用的是/clear 来完成这个工作的，这里和对应的不兼容的，这个机制和/clear 。clear这里会更换对应的session_id的\" (YES, using /clear, incompatible with current mechanism, /clear changes session_id)\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Fix the `/clear` compatibility issue: when Claude Code's `/clear` command fires, it generates a new session_id and triggers `01-session-start` hook again. The current init-lock + PID mechanism only handles the initial proxy startup, not mid-session session_id changes. Need a mechanism to handle re-trace-init within the same running proxy process.\n\n8. Current Work:\n   The user just revealed that the session_id mismatch is caused by Claude Code's `/clear` command. When `/clear` is used:\n   1. Claude Code generates a NEW session_id (e.g., `fa456378`)\n   2. The `01-session-start` hook fires again with the new session_id\n   3. But there's no .init-pid file (already consumed at startup)\n   4. trace-init goes via broadcast (no proxy_pid)\n   5. May route to the wrong proxy → sessionID mismatch\n\n   The backend log confirms:\n   ```\n   18:33:21 PID route session=ae44a20e → pid=4276  ✓ (initial startup works)\n   18:33:36 trace-init: session=fa456378 → pid=7364 (broadcast)  ✗ (/clear session goes to wrong proxy)\n   ```\n\n   The user said: \"对的，我这里使用的是/clear 来完成这个工作的，这里和对应的不兼容的，这个机制和/clear 。clear这里会更换对应的session_id的\"\n\n   Uncommitted change: The guard relaxation in `reverse.go` (replaced strict rejection with debug log) has NOT been committed yet.\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Design a fix for the `/clear` compatibility issue. When the same proxy process receives a second trace-init (from `/clear` generating a new session_id), it should:\n   - Accept the new session_id (guard already relaxed)\n   - But the routing problem remains: the hook can't provide proxy_pid because .init-pid was already consumed\n   \n   Possible approaches:\n   - Have the proxy re-write .init-pid after each successful trace-init (so subsequent /clear sessions can use it)\n   - Use a persistent identifier for the proxy (not just one-time PID file)\n   - Have the backend remember which proxy handled the previous session and route to the same one\n   \n   The user's exact quote: \"对的，我这里使用的是/clear 来完成这个工作的，这里和对应的不兼容的，这个机制和/clear 。clear这里会更换对应的session_id的\"\n</summary>"}
