oject_slug` in request body but auto-detects via `trace.MachineID()` and `trace.ExtractProjectSlug()` when empty — this is fine, no changes needed\n     - `OnTraceInitDone` callback exists for init-lock release\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - **Edit tool whitespace mismatch on main.go**: First attempt to add env var failed because `old_string` had wrong whitespace. Fixed by re-reading exact file content with `cat -A` to see tabs vs spaces.\n   - **Edit tool whitespace mismatch on base.sh**: Similar issue — file used 2-space indentation, not tabs. Fixed by re-reading exact content.\n   - **Test failures after proxy_handler.go rewrite**: Old tests sent `machine_id`/`project_slug` without `proxy_pid`, got 400 \"proxy_pid is required\". Fixed by completely rewriting tests to match new PID-only routing logic.\n   - **User rejected affinity routing and broadcast**: User said \"还广播探测，你在做玩具么？？\". Fixed by stripping all fallback tiers, keeping only PID-based routing.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - **SOLVED**: `/clear` compatibility — `CLAUDE_TAP_PROXY_PID` env var survives `/clear` because `/clear` only resets session_id within Claude Code, doesn't restart the process\n   - **SOLVED**: Concurrent proxy routing — each proxy injects its own PID, hooks always know their proxy\n   - **SOLVED**: Removed all non-deterministic routing (affinity, broadcast, session binding fallback)\n   - **VERIFIED**: All backend tests pass (6/6 trace-init tests), integration tests pass, compilation succeeds\n   - Pre-existing test failures in `tests/e2e` (missing fixture files) and `tests/sse` (usage normalization bug) are unrelated to these changes\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - \"这颗可行么？？？？这么可以的呢？？？？不理解的呢？？这样不是确定的东西还做什么呢？？还广播探测，你在做玩具么？？\" — Strong rejection of non-deterministic routing approaches (affinity, broadcast). Demanded certainty.\n   - \"上一个版本做了什么东西的呢？？？\" — Asked what the previous version (before changes) did.\n   - \"你确定么？\" — Asked for confirmation (triggered this summary).\n\n7. Pending 