[2026-06-07 21:04:29] [INFO] [PostToolBatch] Input: {"session_id":"5a952b88-dbcf-40a5-820e-fed7478f0486","transcript_path":"C:\\Users\\Administrator\\.claude\\projects\\D--CodeDevelopment-CodeProject-claude-hk\\5a952b88-dbcf-40a5-820e-fed7478f0486.jsonl","cwd":"D:\\CodeDevelopment\\CodeProject\\claude-hk\\claude_tap_plus","permission_mode":"plan","effort":{"level":"medium"},"hook_event_name":"PostToolBatch","tool_calls":[{"tool_name":"Agent","tool_input":{"description":"Explore init-lock and init-pid mechanism","prompt":"I need to understand the complete init-lock + init-pid file mechanism in this project, and how the trace-init flow works end-to-end.\n\nSearch thoroughly for:\n\n1. In `claude_tap_plus/cmd/claude-tap/main.go`:\n   - The init-lock (mkdir) mechanism - where it's acquired, what it guards, when it's released\n   - The init-pid file writing\n   - The `initDone` channel and `OnTraceInitDone` callback\n   - The select wait for initDone\n   - The `OnSessionInit` callback\n   - The `childEnv` construction and what env vars are injected\n\n2. In `claude_tap_plus/internal/proxy/reverse.go`:\n   - The `OnTraceInitDone` callback field - where it's defined and invoked\n   - The `handleTraceInit` function - what it does\n   - The `OnSessionInit` callback field\n\n3. In `claude_tap_plus/internal/backend/api/proxy_handler.go`:\n   - The TraceInit handler - full implementation\n   - The register/unregister handlers\n\n4. In `.claude/hooks/01-session-start/base.sh`:\n   - The init_trace_path function - full implementation\n\n5. Search for ALL references to:\n   - `init-lock`, `initLockPath`, `.init-lock`\n   - `init-pid`, `initPIDPath`, `.init-pid`\n   - `initDone`, `OnTraceInitDone`\n   - `CLAUDE_TAP_PROXY_PID`, `CLAUDE_TAP_PROXY_URL`\n   - `trace-init`, `traceInit`\n\nReport the exact line numbers and code for each finding. Be very thorough - I need to understand every piece that touches this mechanism.","subagent_type":"Explore"},"tool_use_id":"call_b2edf798307a4a6fbadfda99","tool_response":[{"type":"text","text":"\n## Complete Init-Lock + Init-PID File Mechanism Analysis\n\nBased on my thorough analysis of the code, here's the complete end-to-end flow of the init-lock + init-pid file mechanism and trace-init process:\n\n### 1. **Init-Lock Mechanism in `claude_tap_plus/cmd/claude-tap/main.go`**\n\n**Lock Acquisition (Lines 273-286):**\n```go\ninitLockPath := filepath.Join(BaseDir(), \".init-lock\")\ninitPIDPath := filepath.Join(BaseDir(), \".init-pid\")\n\n// Get init lock (blocking wait)\nfor {\n    if err := os.Mkdir(initLockPath, 0o755); err == nil {\n        logger.Info(\"main\", \"init lock acquired\")\n        break\n    }\n    logger.Debug(\"main\", \"init lock busy, waiting...\")\n    time.Sleep(100 * time.Millisecond)\n}\n// Ensure lock is released on exit\ndefer os.RemoveAll(initLockPath)\n```\n\n**PID File Writing (Lines 289-292):**\n```go\nif err := os.WriteFile(initPIDPath, []byte(strconv.Itoa(os.Getpid())), 0o644); err != nil {\n    logger.Warn(\"main\", \"write init-pid failed: %v\", err)\n}\nlogger.Info(\"main\", \"init-pid written: %d\", os.Getpid())\n```\n\n**What it guards:** The init lock ensures only one proxy can be in the initialization phase at a time, preventing race conditions when multiple proxies try to initialize trace tracking simultaneously.\n\n### 2. **InitDone Channel and Callbacks**\n\n**InitDone Channel Creation (Line 295):**\n```go\ninitDone := make(chan struct{}, 1)\n```\n\n**OnTraceInitDone Callback Registration (Lines 296-301):**\n```go\nrp.OnTraceInitDone = func() {\n    select {\n    case initDone <- struct{}{}:\n    default:\n    }\n}\n```\n\n**OnSessionInit Callback Registration (Lines 304-309):**\n```go\nrp.OnSessionInit = func(sessionID, projectSlug string) {\n    key := ProxySessionKey(projectSlug, sessionID)\n    if err := RegisterProxySession(key, time.Now().Format(time.RFC3339)); err != nil {\n        logger.Warn(\"main\", \"register proxy session failed: %v\", err)\n    }\n}\n```\n\n### 3. **ChildEnv Construction and PID Injection**\n\n**Base ChildEnv Creation (Line 328):**\n```go\nchildEnv := config.BuildChildEnv(&config.ClaudeClient, proxyURL)\n```\n\n**Proxy PID Injection (Lines 330-331):**\n```go\n// Inject proxy PID to child process environment (hook can read directly, solves /clear after .init-pid consumed)\nchildEnv = append(childEnv, \"CLAUDE_TAP_PROXY_PID=\"+strconv.Itoa(os.Getpid()))\n```\n\n**Auth Information Injection (Lines 333-340):**\n```go\nif resolved.APIKey != \"\" {\n    childEnv = removeEnvVar(childEnv, \"ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN\")\n    childEnv = append(childEnv, \"ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=\"+resolved.APIKey)\n} else if resolved.AuthToken != \"\" {\n    childEnv = removeEnvVar(childEnv, \"ANTHROPIC_API_KEY\")\n    childEnv = append(childEnv, \"ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN=\"+resolved.AuthToken)\n}\n```\n\n### 4. **Select Wait for InitDone (Lines 364-373)**\n```go\n// Wait for trace-init to complete before releasing init lock, allowing next proxy to start\nselect {\ncase <-initDone:\n    logger.Info(\"main\", \"trace-init received, init lock releasing\")\ncase <-time.After(30 * time.Second):\n    logger.Warn(\"main\", \"trace-init timeout (30s), releasing init lock anyway\")\n}\n// Delete PID file (if hook didn't delete)\nos.Remove(initPIDPath)\n// Release init lock (defer will also execute, here early release so next proxy doesn't wait)\nos.RemoveAll(initLockPath)\n```\n\n### 5. **OnTraceInitDone Callback in `claude_tap_plus/internal/proxy/reverse.go`**\n\n**Callback Field Definition (Line 34):**\n```go\nOnTraceInitDone func() // trace-init processing complete callback (notify main.go to release init lock)\n```\n\n**Callback Invocation in handleTraceInit (Lines 558-561):**\n```go\n// Notify main.go: trace-init processing complete, can release init lock\nif p.OnTraceInitDone != nil {\n    p.OnTraceInitDone()\n}\n```\n\n### 6. **HandleTraceInit Function (Lines 489-568)**\n\n**Session Binding Logic (Lines 514-518):**\n```go\n// Concurrent routing guaranteed by init lock + PID file, allows session rebinding (old session结束后可更新)\nif p.sessionID != \"\" && p.sessionID != req.SessionID {\n    logger.Debug(\"proxy\", \"trace-init: rebinding session %s -> %s\", p.sessionID, req.SessionID)\n}\n```\n\n**Trace Writer Creation (Lines 535-550):**\n```go\n// Create session-specific Trace writer\ntracePath := trace.NewSessionTracePath(p.baseDir, machineID, projectSlug, req.SessionID)\nwriter, err := trace.NewTraceWriter(tracePath)\np.sessionID = req.SessionID   // Record current session ID\np.projectSlug = projectSlug   // Record current project identifier\nif err != nil {\n    logger.Error(\"proxy\", \"trace-init: failed to create writer: %v\", err)\n    http.Error(w, \"failed to create trace file\", http.StatusInternalServerError)\n    return\n}\n```\n\n**OnSessionInit Callback Invocation (Lines 554-556):**\n```go\n// Notify external to register proxy.json\nif p.OnSessionInit != nil {\n    p.OnSessionInit(req.SessionID, projectSlug)\n}\n```\n\n### 7. **TraceInit Handler in `claude_tap_plus/internal/backend/api/proxy_handler.go`**\n\n**Handler Definition (Lines 132-191):**\n```go\n// TraceInit forwards trace-init requests to specified proxy.\n// POST /api/proxy/trace-init\n// Routing logic: precise routing to target proxy through proxy_pid (environment variable injected).\n// PID from CLAUDE_TAP_PROXY_PID environment variable, injected by proxy at startup, still valid after /clear.\n```\n\n**PID-based Routing (Lines 166-168):**\n```go\nh.mu.RLock()\nproxyURL, found := h.proxies[tiReq.ProxyPID]\nh.mu.RUnlock()\n```\n\n**Relay to Target Proxy (Line 177):**\n```go\n// Forward to target proxy\nresp, err := relayTraceInit(proxyURL, body)\n```\n\n**Session Binding (Lines 185-187):**\n```go\n// Bind session (for cleanup on unregister)\nh.mu.Lock()\nh.bindSession(tiReq.ProxyPID, tiReq.SessionID, proxyURL)\nh.mu.Unlock()\n```\n\n### 8. **InitTracePath Function in `.claude/hooks/01-session-start/base.sh`**\n\n**PID Acquisition Logic (Lines 105-115):**\n```bash\n# Get proxy PID: priority from environment variable (still valid after /clear), then from init-pid file (first startup)\nlocal tap_pid=\"${CLAUDE_TAP_PROXY_PID:-}\"\nif [ -n \"$tap_pid\" ]; then\n    log \"INFO\" \"Proxy PID from env: $tap_pid\"\nelse\n    local init_pid_file=\"$HOME/.claude-tap-plus/.init-pid\"\n    if [ -f \"$init_pid_file\" ]; then\n        tap_pid=$(cat \"$init_pid_file\" 2>/dev/null)\n        rm -f \"$init_pid_file\"\n        log \"INFO\" \"Init PID consumed: ${tap_pid:-empty}\"\n    fi\nfi\n```\n\n**Backend Forwarding (Lines 124-128):**\n```bash\n# Forward trace-init to proxy through backend (PID precise routing, no guessing)\nif [ -z \"$tap_pid\" ]; then\n    log \"WARN\" \"Trace init skipped: no proxy PID available\"\n    return 0\nfi\n\nlocal result\nresult=$(_call_backend \"/api/proxy/trace-init\" \"{\n    \\\"session_id\\\":\\\"$sid\\\",\n    \\\"proxy_pid\\\":\\\"$tap_pid\\\",\n    \\\"transcript_path\\\":\\\"$safe_transcript_path\\\"\n}\")\n```\n\n**Trace Path Storage (Lines 131-135):**\n```bash\nif [ -n \"$result\" ]; then\n    __LAST_TRACE_PATH=$(echo \"$result\" | jq -r '.trace_path // \"\"' 2>/dev/null)\n    log \"INFO\" \"Trace initialized: ${__LAST_TRACE_PATH:-unknown}\"\nelse\n    log \"DEBUG\" \"Trace init failed (backend call returned empty)\"\nfi\n```\n\n### 9. **End-to-End Flow Summary**\n\n1. **Proxy Startup:** \n   - Acquires `.init-lock` directory (blocking)\n   - Writes `.init-pid` file with its PID\n   - Injects `CLAUDE_TAP_PROXY_PID` into child process environment\n\n2. **Claude Code Starts:**\n   - Hook runs `init_trace_path()` function\n   - Gets PID from env (preferred) or `.init-pid` file\n   - Deletes `.init-pid` file after consumption\n   - Calls backend `/api/proxy/trace-init` with session info and proxy PID\n\n3. **Backend Processing:**\n   - Looks up proxy PID in registered proxies\n   - Forwards request to proxy's `_internal/trace-init` endpoint\n   - Binds session to proxy for cleanup\n\n4. **Proxy Processing:**\n   - Creates trace writer for the session\n   - Sets session ID and project slug\n   - Invokes `OnSessionInit` callback to register session\n   - Invokes `OnTraceInitDone` callback to signal completion\n\n5. **Lock Release:**\n   - Main proxy receives signal from `initDone` channel\n   - Releases `.init-lock` directory\n   - Next proxy can now acquire lock\n\nThis mechanism ensures serialized trace initialization while maintaining session binding and proper cleanup across multiple proxy instances."}]},{"tool_name":"Agent","tool_input":{"description":"Explore hook script infrastructure","prompt":"I need to understand the hook script infrastructure that supports the trace-init flow.\n\nSearch thoroughly for:\n\n1. `.claude/hooks/lib/backend.sh` - the `_call_backend`, `_backend_available` functions. How does the hook call the backend? What tools does it use (curl, wget, etc.)?\n\n2. `.claude/hooks/base.sh` - the shared infrastructure. Look for `hook_output`, `json_get`, any HTTP call utilities.\n\n3. `.claude/lib/config.sh` - `load_backend_config()`, how `$BACKEND_URL` is set.\n\n4. Check if there are any existing utilities in the hook infrastructure for making direct HTTP calls (not just through backend). Look for curl, wget, or any HTTP functions.\n\n5. Search for `curl` usage across ALL `.claude/` shell scripts to understand the HTTP calling patterns.\n\n6. Check `.claude/hooks/29-session-end/base.sh` for how it calls the backend (to understand the pattern).\n\nReport exact file paths, line numbers, and relevant code snippets.","subagent_type":"Explore"},"tool_use_id":"call_3135e72370ba480caa6281bd","tool_response":[{"type":"text","text":"\nBased on my comprehensive search through the codebase, I can now provide you with a detailed understanding of the hook script infrastructure that supports the trace-init flow. Here's what I found:\n\n## Hook Script Infrastructure Analysis\n\n### Key Findings\n\n**Important Discovery**: The actual hook script infrastructure (`.claude/hooks/lib/backend.sh`, `.claude/hooks/base.sh`, etc.) does **not exist** in this codebase. However, the tests reference these files, indicating they should exist for the hook system to work.\n\n### 1. **Backend Communication Infrastructure (Go Code)**\n\nThe backend communication is implemented in Go code, not shell scripts:\n\n**File**: `internal/backend/api/proxy_handler.go`\n- **`TraceInit` method (lines 136-191)**: Handles trace-init requests\n- Uses precise routing via `proxy_pid` from environment variable `CLAUDE_TAP_PROXY_PID`\n- Forwards requests to the correct proxy instance\n- **HTTP client pattern**: Uses standard Go `http.Client` for backend calls\n\n**File**: `internal/backend/api/request.go`\n- **`TraceInitRequest` struct (lines 59-64)**: Defines the request structure\n- Contains: `session_id`, `proxy_pid`, `transcript_path`\n\n### 2. **Proxy Infrastructure**\n\n**File**: `internal/proxy/reverse.go`\n- **`handleTraceInit` method (lines 490-568)**: Creates trace writers\n- **Pattern**: Creates session-specific trace files at `tracePath`\n- **HTTP handler**: `/_internal/trace-init` endpoint\n\n### 3. **HTTP Calling Patterns in Go**\n\nThe codebase uses **standard Go HTTP client** for all backend communication:\n```go\n// From proxy_handler.go line 242-249\nclient := &http.Client{}\nreq, err := http.NewRequest(\"POST\", proxyURL+\"/_internal/trace-init\", bytes.NewReader(body))\nif err != nil {\n    return nil, err\n}\nreq.Header.Set(\"Content-Type\", \"application/json\")\nresp, err := client.Do(req)\n```\n\n### 4. **Test Evidence of Missing Infrastructure**\n\n**File**: `tests/shell/b7_backend_sh_test.sh` (lines 13-14, 63)\n```bash\nBACKEND_SH=\"$PROJECT_DIR/.claude/skills/backend.sh\"\nBACKEND_CONF=\"$PROJECT_DIR/.claude/backend.conf\"\n```\n\nThis test references files that don't exist in the current codebase:\n- `.claude/skills/backend.sh`\n- `.claude/backend.conf`\n\n### 5. **Expected Hook Infrastructure (Based on Tests)**\n\nFrom the test files, the expected infrastructure should include:\n\n**Functions in `.claude/skills/backend.sh`**:\n- `_load_backend_url()` - Loads backend URL from config\n- `_backend_available()` - Checks backend availability (2s timeout)\n- `_call_backend()` - Makes HTTP calls to backend (5s timeout)\n- `_get_session_id()` - Reads from `CLAUDE_SESSION_ID` env var\n- `update_issue_status()` - Updates issue status via backend\n- `_status_to_label()` - Maps internal status to GitHub labels\n- `_sync_github_label()` - Syncs GitHub labels\n\n**From test `b7_backend_sh_test.sh`** (lines 70-75):\n```bash\nfor fn in _load_backend_url _backend_available _call_backend _get_session_id update_issue_status _status_to_label _sync_github_label; do\n    if ! type \"$fn\" &>/dev/null; then\n        echo \"FAIL: function $fn not defined after source\"\n        return 1\n    fi\ndone\n```\n\n### 6. **Configuration Pattern**\n\n**Expected file**: `.claude/backend.conf`\n- Simple format: `BACKEND_URL=http://localhost:8080`\n- Checked by `_load_backend_url()` function\n\n### 7. **Trace Init Flow**\n\nThe complete flow is:\n1. **SessionStart hook** → calls `/api/proxy/trace-init` with `session_id`, `proxy_pid`\n2. **Backend** → forwards to correct proxy using `proxy_pid` routing\n3. **Proxy** → creates trace writer, responds with trace path\n4. **SessionEnd hook** → calls `/api/session/close` to finalize\n\n### 8. **HTTP Utilities**\n\nBased on the test patterns, the missing shell infrastructure should include:\n- **`curl` or `wget`** for HTTP calls\n- **JSON parsing** (possibly using `jq` or manual parsing)\n- **Timeout handling** (2-5 seconds as per tests)\n- **Error handling** with silent failures\n\n### Summary\n\nThe hook script infrastructure you're looking for is **missing** from this codebase. However, based on the test files, it should exist at:\n- `.claude/skills/backend.sh` - Main backend communication functions\n- `.claude/backend.conf` - Backend URL configuration\n- `.claude/hooks/lib/backend.sh` - Backend utilities (referenced but not found)\n- `.claude/hooks/base.sh` - Shared hook infrastructure (referenced but not found)\n\nThe actual implementation uses Go HTTP clients, but the hook system expects shell script utilities for making HTTP calls to the backend."}]}]}
