 Add CLAUDE_TAP_PROXY_URL env var injection\n\n9. Implementation:\n   - main.go: Removed init-lock (mkdir), init-pid file writing, initDone channel, OnTraceInitDone callback, select wait. Added CLAUDE_TAP_PROXY_URL injection. Removed unused `filepath` import.\n   - reverse.go: Removed OnTraceInitDone field and callback invocation. Updated guard comment.\n   - base.sh: Rewrote init_trace_path() to read CLAUDE_TAP_PROXY_URL from env and curl proxy directly.\n\n10. Had Edit tool whitespace mismatches - had to use python for reverse.go edit and verify exact tab indentation.\n\n11. All tests passed (6/6), compilation succeeded.\n\n12. Git push with two commits:\n    - `608e79c` refactor: Go code changes (5 files, +92/-202)\n    - `167671e` refactor: hook script changes (1 file, +9/-28)\n\n13. User asked to build the package - built successfully as claude-tap-plus.exe (17MB).\n\n14. User reported a bug: \"出bug了，一直阻塞不可以进行对应的一个proxy上线的\" - proxy blocking and can't come online.\n\n15. I checked hook logs and found: `Trace init skipped: no proxy URL in env` - CLAUDE_TAP_PROXY_URL was empty.\n\n16. Checked proxy-side logs and found the user was running the OLD binary (`claued_tap_plus.exe` from 18:47) which still had init-lock mechanism. The old binary's init-lock was blocking for 30 seconds waiting for OnTraceInitDone.\n\n17. User asked \"新build的逻辑是什么呢？\" - I explained the new flow.\n\n18. User showed the current base.sh script and asked me to look at it.\n\n19. User's last request: \"我需要加入对应的一个log的，输出到我的log文件里面的\" - wants to add more logging to init_trace_path() to output to the log file.\n\nThe current state is that I was about to add more detailed logging to the init_trace_path() function in base.sh, but was interrupted by the compaction request.\n\nKey files:\n- claude_tap_plus/cmd/claude-tap/main.go - removed init-lock, added env var injection\n- claude_tap_plus/internal/proxy/reverse.go - removed OnTraceInitDone\n- .claude/hooks/01-session-start/base.sh - rewrote init_trace_path()\n- claude_tap_plus/internal/backend/api/proxy_handler.go - PID-only routing (from previous session)\n- claude_tap_plus/internal/backend/api/request.go - simplified TraceInitRequest (from previous session)\n- claude_tap_plus/tests/backend/proxy_trace_init_test.go - rewritten tests (from previous session)\n\nPending task: Add logging to init_trace_path() in base.sh.\n</analysis>\n\n<summary>\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   - **Original request (from previous session)**: Fix trace-init routing bugs where concurrent proxy instances send session initialization to the WRONG proxy process. Two scenarios: initial startup and `/clear` compatibility.\n   - **Main request in this session**: Simplify the init-lock + init-pid file mechanism by using environment variables `CLAUDE_TAP_PROXY_PID` and `CLAUDE_TAP_PROXY_URL` directly, so the hook can call the proxy without backend relay.\n   - **Current pending request**: Add more detailed logging to `init_trace_path()` function in `base.sh`, outputting to the log file.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - **Process tree environment variable inheritance**: Proxy → Claude Code (child) → hook script (child of Claude Code). Env vars flow down and survive `/clear`.\n   - **`CLAUDE_TAP_PROXY_PID` + `CLAUDE_TAP_PROXY_URL`**: Two env vars injected by proxy into child processes. PID for identification, URL for direct connection.\n   - **Direct proxy call**: Hook reads `CLAUDE_TAP_PROXY_URL` from env and `curl`s proxy's `/_internal/trace-init` directly — no backend relay needed.\n   - **Removed mechanisms**: init-lock (mkdir atomic), init-pid file (one-time consumption), OnTraceInitDone callback, initDone channel, traceMu serial lock, 3-level fallback routing, broadcast probing.\n   - **Backend and proxy are separate processes**: `claude_tap_plus.exe backend -port 8080` and `claude_tap_plus.exe --tap-profile glm --claude` are two independent processes. Proxy registers itself with backend via `POST /api/proxy/register`. Backend 